### R1-COR-MAJ-001 (correctness) — --restore PUT shape mismatch

**Bug:** scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore mode sends the GitHub GET-response format `enforce_admins` object (`{"url":"...","enabled":true}`) directly to the branch-protection PUT endpoint, which documents the field as a plain boolean. Same shape mismatch on `required_status_checks` (GET returns `{contexts, strict, url, checks}`; PUT accepts `{contexts, strict}`). This causes HTTP 422 and breaks the <30-min rollback SLO.

**Fix:** in scripts/enable-required-check.sh restore_branch_protection() function, transform the captured `before` JSON into PUT-compatible format before the PUT call. Use a Python heredoc (mirroring the `python3 - <<PY` pattern used elsewhere in the script): extract the boolean from `enforce_admins.enabled`; strip `url` and `checks` sub-fields from `required_status_checks`; normalise `restrictions` to null if absent or `{users, teams, apps}` shape. Pass the transformed JSON as the PUT payload. Add a test case in tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh that verifies the transform produces the expected shape (read a fixture before-JSON in GET shape, run the transform helper, assert PUT-shape output).

