{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"R1-COR-CRIT-001|R1-COR-MAJ-001|R1-COR-MAJ-002|SAFE-001|SAFE-002|SAFE-003|MAJ-TF-001|MAJ-AC-001|D-044|Tracked-forward items|operator step 7|Acceptance criteria\" docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md docs/DECISIONS.md STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"docs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:10:- **D-044** — reserved for slice 024B: `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder`) operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:49:   **Meaningful-content format spec (closes 024A R5 R5-NEW-MAJ-002 safety + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-001 safety/completeness regex prose mismatch + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-001 completeness regex file-scoping).** TF-024X references — whether they appear in STATUS.md (the `onboarded-operator-bump` row in \"Tracked-forward items\") or in DISPATCH-NOTE (the `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` reference) — MUST contain a line matching this regex literally:\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:65:   The check is a hard predecessor for slice 024C — 024C does not open until the enforcement script is committed + green AND covers all four CI behaviours (the three named cascade-status check-paths + the fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised values). Closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 + 024A R2 NEW-MAJ-001 + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness — third cascade-status value) + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 (safety — bypass via concurrent invocation + conflict-declaration) + 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety — bare-prefix TF-row stub bypass) + 024A R5 R5-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety — meaningful-content format spec) + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-001 (safety + completeness — regex non-whitespace anchor + file-agnostic scoping) + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-003 (safety — fail-closed default).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:70:7. **Per-adopter rollback is single-operator-doable.** Each cascade slice ships a rollback procedure: `enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` reverts branch protection to the captured before-state, and the adopter wrapper PR can be reverted via standard `git revert`. Rollback time SLO: **<30 minutes from operator decision to merge-restored state — claimed only after slice 024B closes with a demonstrated real-repo round-trip on a throw-away test repo (not a dry-run mock).** The SLO is aspirational at 024A merge; 024B's acceptance criterion in §6 makes the round-trip a hard predecessor for 024C. Documented per cascade slice. Closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:139:   - STATUS.md row update (cascade-slice progress) — and, when `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`, a `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row in \"Tracked-forward items\".\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:144:5. **FLA pilot safety findings reviewed** — single line in DISPATCH-NOTE (template lands in 024B's D-044): `FLA pilot safety findings reviewed: [none new since <last slice's check date> | <link to finding>]`. This is **not** an FLA precondition (invariant 4 still holds); it is a check that the cascade slice author has looked at the FLA pilot state before opening the slice, so safety discoveries don't silently accumulate between slices. Closes 024A R1 MIN-SAFE-005.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:164:D-044 ratifies this script's operational contract: bootstrap-only (refuses CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true per D-035 symmetry), validates `--scp-sha` against the SCP main HEAD at invocation time (warns if it's not main HEAD; refuses to emit if it's a non-existent SHA), and emits a manifest file `MANIFEST.json` listing every file emitted + its SHA256 for audit.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:203:| Slice | Deliverable | Acceptance criteria | Tier | Dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:206:| 024B | `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` + `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` + `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode + `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` (CI enforcement of invariant 2 — closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 + 024A R2 NEW-MAJ-001 + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 correctness + safety + 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 safety + 024A R6 R6-NEW-MAJ-002/003 safety) + scaffolder unit tests | Scaffolder emits a known-fixture wrapper that schema-validates against the canonical wrapper shape from ADOPT-001 §12; `--restore` round-trip via captured before-state restores branch-protection state byte-for-byte **on a real throw-away test repo** (not a dry-run mock — closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003); `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` parses DISPATCH-NOTE `cascade-status:` field and implements all four CI behaviours per invariant 2 — **fail-closed default** (absent or unrecognised value → exit non-zero); for `onboarded`: requires log entry + target match; for `onboarded-operator-bump`: requires log entry + target match + `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` STATUS.md row matching invariant 2's **regex format spec literally** (file-agnostic; `\\S` non-whitespace anchor at description start; ≥20 char total); for `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`: requires `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference (in DISPATCH-NOTE) matching the same regex spec literally AND **asserts log file was NOT modified** (closes the R3 safety bypass + R4 safety stub bypass + R6 safety regex/whitespace + file-scoping bypasses); D-044 filed. **All three components (scaffolder + --restore + check-invocation-log-entry.sh covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C.** | Codex executor | Per WP-SCP-022 dispatch contract |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:227:| **R-024-07** | Renovate misses a cohort adopter (e.g. adopter has Renovate disabled). | The cascade slice surfaces this in DISPATCH-NOTE by declaring `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`. Operator-driven SHA pin bump PR is acceptable as a **temporary** unblock, but the cascade slice MUST file a forward TF (`TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>`) **as a STATUS.md \"Tracked-forward items\" row matching invariant 2's regex spec literally** (status field ∈ {open, pending, in-progress, closed} + description starting with a non-whitespace character (`\\S` anchor) + ≥20 chars total — bare-prefix stubs and all-whitespace descriptions fail the CI check per invariant 2; closes 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 safety + 024A R7 R7-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness) + R7-NEW-MAJ-003 (completeness) — pre-R6 paraphrase swept at R-024-07). The `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI script verifies STATUS.md contains the matching TF row + regex-spec match when DISPATCH-NOTE declares `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`. The adopter is **not credited toward Threshold A** until that TF closes + a real Renovate cycle has merged + observed clean. This distinguishes adopters that genuinely exercise automated version-skew tolerance from those that satisfy the letter of the criterion via a one-off operator action. Closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-004 + 024A R2 NEW-MIN-002 + 024A R3 R3-NEW-MAJ-001 (correctness — third cascade-status value enumerated) + 024A R4 R4-NEW-MAJ-002 (safety — meaningful-content gate). T-024-04 mitigation still applies. | Each cascade slice |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:233:| **R-024-13** | Plan-doc commits to scaffolder shape before scaffolder is implemented. | Plan-doc is v0.1. Scaffolder's ratifying decision (D-044) lands at 024B with the implementation. Plan-doc shape may be amended at 024B if implementation surfaces a better shape. | 024A → 024B |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:237:## 8. Acceptance criteria + Threshold A\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:242:- D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reserved (not assigned in this slice).\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:259:| **D-044** | 024B | `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` operational contract — bootstrap-only / no-CI guards (D-035 symmetry); `--scp-sha` validation against SCP main HEAD; `--default-branch` flag + template substitution; `MANIFEST.json` audit emission. Adopter-template versioning (template SHA captured in scaffolder output for forensic traceability). Invocation-log convention extension: scaffolder writes a \"rendered-template\" log entry alongside `enable-required-check.sh`'s branch-protection log. Ratifies invariants 2 + 3 + 10 in code form. |\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:263:**Codex-executor reservation guard.** Per the `docs/DECISIONS.md` header reservation block, Codex executors dispatched for any WP-SCP-024 implementation slice must NOT assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that slice. The reservation pattern mirrors WP-SCP-022's D-021 reservation guard + WP-SCP-023's D-041/D-042/D-043 reservation guard.\ndocs/plans/WP-SCP-024-estate-cascade.md:271:3. **`enable-required-check.sh --restore` test surface** — the rollback mode lands at 024B. How is it tested without actually mutating an estate repo? **Resolution path (closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003):** Q3 closes only when 024B's acceptance criterion in §6 is met — i.e. a real-repo round-trip on a throw-away test repo (NOT a dry-run mock). Until that demonstration is complete, invariant 7's <30-min rollback SLO is aspirational and 024C MUST NOT open.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-044 filed at WP-SCP-024 024B; D-045 / D-046 remain reserved; estate cascade)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 is reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:43:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:81:| D-034 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020F renovate-tag-protection (parallel ruleset to D-030's `v*` ruleset, targeting `refs/tags/renovate/v*`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001: `renovate/v*` tag series unprotected — an attacker with push access could silently re-point `renovate/v1.0.0` to a malicious commit and cascade adversarial Renovate config to every estate adopter on their next scheduled run. The 020J ruleset matches `refs/tags/v*` (literal v-prefix at start) only. New ruleset `scp-tag-protection-renovate-v` applies same protections (deletion / non_fast_forward / update blocked, `enforcement: active`, `bypass_actors: []`). Configured via `scripts/configure-020f-renovate-tag-protection.sh` (idempotent, jq-based JSON construction to eliminate heredoc-interpolation injection surface, multi-property post-creation verification). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md` \"Tag protection — renovate/v* pattern\" section. Symmetric with D-030 in posture and rationale; the only material difference is the tag-pattern segment. The `renovate/v*` series carries equal supply-chain weight as `v*` because every adopter that extends the preset cascades changes from the renovate-pattern tag to their own gate config | ACCEPTED | The 020J ruleset's `v*` literal-prefix pattern is by-design narrow; broadening to all release-track tags would require a separate ruleset per pattern. Renovate's preset shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default#renovate/v1.0.0` is the standard Renovate adopter onboarding shape; without ruleset protection, the entire preset trust chain is rooted in mutable tag refs. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged identically to D-030: the same admin who owns @jrnb2024 is the one publishing tags; the protection guards against accidental force-push, not against malicious admin action. Quarterly review cadence (2026-07-30 in STATUS.md \"Open scheduled follow-ups\") covers both rulesets together. Identified by 020F R1 safety review (workflow run dispatched 2026-04-30 evening) — surfaced under the no-silent-descope governance invariant after fix-round-1 closed the substantive R1 findings |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B operational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; future wrapper-shape changes land in the template + propagate via Renovate SHA bumps. (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state and now validates that captured before-state as a legitimate GitHub branch-protection payload (required_status_checks object, enforce_admins.enabled boolean, required_pull_request_reviews object-or-null, restrictions object-or-null). Restore mode captures the actually-observed current branch-protection state immediately before PUT, then logs the observed degraded state separately so the audit trail shows both the target good-state and the broken pre-restore state. New safety check (forward mode only): resolves the `policy-check` workflow id, then refuses to invoke unless the repo has at least one successful `policy-check` workflow run in the last 60 days; if no `policy-check` workflow is registered, or no successful runs exist in the 60-day window, it exits with the existing cold-start error unless `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` is set. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:7:**Decision filed:** D-044 (scaffolder operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension + `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:36:| `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo | `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` | NOT a dry-run mock per plan-doc invariant 7 SLO honesty + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003. Throw-away test repo (e.g. `jrnb2024/scp-024b-restore-test`); capture before-state via existing log entry shape; mutate branch protection; restore via `--restore`; verify byte-for-byte match. Evidence captured for D-044 ratification. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:39:| D-044 filing | `docs/DECISIONS.md` row | Scaffolder operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension + `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode semantics. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:71:## Acceptance criteria\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:76:- [ ] `--restore` round-trip via captured before-state restores branch-protection state byte-for-byte **on a real throw-away test repo** (not a dry-run mock — closes 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:82:- [ ] D-044 filed.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:119:2. **Codex Tier 3 executor** (direct `codex exec --model gpt-5.4-mini` with reasoning-effort medium) — implementation: scaffolder + template + `--restore` extension + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests + ADOPT-001 §12 break-glass + D-044 row + STATUS.md update. Capture work-package + stdout to `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/codex-dispatch-manual-audit.log`.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:124:7. **Operator real-repo `--restore` round-trip demo** (operator-interactive; standard `gh` PAT; throw-away test repo). Evidence captured into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md`. Demo blocks slice merge per plan-doc §6 acceptance criterion + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:133:| 2 | Codex executor (direct `codex exec`): scaffolder + template + `--restore` + CI script + unit tests + ADOPT-001 §12 + D-044 row + STATUS.md | Codex T3 deviated | ~45–60 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:148:Per `docs/DECISIONS.md` header, D-044 is reserved for this slice. Codex executor MUST NOT assign D-044 to any other decision filed during this slice. The reservation pattern mirrors D-021 (WP-SCP-022) + D-041–043 (WP-SCP-023) + D-044/045/046 (WP-SCP-024 reservation block already in place).\nSTATUS.md:3:**Last updated:** 2026-05-09 (WP-SCP-024 024B - scaffolder + --restore + invocation-log CI; D-044 filed; previous: 2026-05-09 D-035-rules retired)\nSTATUS.md:115:| 2 | #98 | **023B** | Per-repo scorecard emitter + schema (closes D-041). NEW `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1 (MAJOR-pinned per VERSIONING.md D-036). NEW opt-in `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input on `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` (default false; existing adopters see no behaviour change). New separate `attest-scorecard` job with job-scoped OIDC permissions (closes 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001 — workflow-level `id-token: write` would have exposed adopter cloud-IAM trust to ALL runs). 4 fixture pairs (minimal / full / deny-with-waiver / warn-baseline); 12/12 pytest pass. NEVER emits waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema + dedicated pytest scan). v1.1.0 → **v1.2.0** (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). 3-round adversarial review caught 6 unique MAJs. Merged at `5d4341b`; `v1.2.0` tag cut + GitHub release published; release-gate dry-run + post-tag observer both clean. |\nSTATUS.md:119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:137:**Slice 024B remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope unchanged: scaffolder + `--restore` mode + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + D-044 + real-repo rollback round-trip.\nSTATUS.md:143:| 1 | #<scaffolder-PR> | **024B** | D-044 filed; protocol deviation noted (direct codex exec for 024B; cohort cascade 024C-F gated on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure); plan-doc §6 amended with cohort dispatcher precondition; ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure shipped; scaffolder + template + `--restore` + invocation-log CI + tests all live; `--restore` real-repo round-trip evidence PENDING — operator-interactive demo at step 7 of dispatch plan; evidence path `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` to be committed post-demo, pre-merge, per plan-doc §6 acceptance criterion. |\nSTATUS.md:163:## Tracked-forward items from 020C.1\nSTATUS.md:170:## Tracked-forward items from 020D1 (closed in 020H part 3)\nSTATUS.md:176:## Tracked-forward items from 020H part 3\nSTATUS.md:184:## Tracked-forward items from 020H.1\nSTATUS.md:192:## Tracked-forward items from 020H.3 (release-gate)\nSTATUS.md:199:## Tracked-forward items from 020M (supply-chain hash-pinning)\nSTATUS.md:204:## Tracked-forward items from 020N (conflict-gate hash-pinning)\nSTATUS.md:208:## Tracked-forward items from 020L (first rule-RFC dogfood)\nSTATUS.md:214:## Tracked-forward items from 020P (RULE-001 Phase 2)\nSTATUS.md:224:## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-023 023A (plan-doc) + 023B (emitter) + 023C (aggregator)\nSTATUS.md:230:- **TF-023B-003** (low priority): Promote `WARN_BASELINE_RULES` to data-driven manifest per TF-020P-001's scope. Filed at 023B R3 R3-MIN-SAFE-002.\nSTATUS.md:235:- **TF-023C-005** (forward-compat): SCP repo rename/transfer — update the regex anchor in `schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json` + `SCP_WORKFLOW_REF_PREFIX` constant. Filed at 023C R1 safety MAJ-SAFE-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:236:- **TF-023C-006** (low priority): Minimum `scp_version` check on verified emits. An adopter pinning a very old SCP version remains 'verified' since the aggregator is info