d from 1 to 0 (single-operator self-approval is structurally impossible on GitHub); `require_code_owner_reviews` corrected from true to false (same root cause). See D-033 for the operational test path that surfaced these | ACCEPTED | This is the operational closure of the WP-SCP-020 federation primitive — SCP gates itself on its own `main`. Closure of governance B-2 (the original brief was \"convert SCP from advisory auditor to deterministic pre-merge enforcement\"). Required-status-check + enforce_admins=true + required-signed-commits + required-PR-reviews compose into a 4-layer protection: (1) every commit is cryptographically attested, (2) every change runs through the SCP gate, (3) every change has at least one human approval, (4) admin override is OFF. Single-operator self-approval is the bus-factor-1 cost; the 2026-07-21 escalation review is the named re-evaluation moment. The pre-protection canary (020E.a) proved the deny mechanism worked on real PR; flipping to required adds enforcement, not behaviour. Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020D2; preconditions 020J + 020K + 020D1 + 020E.a + USER-GATE-A0 all closed before this slice opens |\n| D-033 | 2026-04-30 | WP-SCP-022 020D2.1 reconciliation: amend D-032's branch-protection shape on the SCP repo to reflect two operational realities surfaced when the first PR (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64) attempted to merge through enforced mode. (a) **Required-check context name correction:** WP-SCP-020 020B(xi) specified `scp/policy-check` as the context name. GitHub Actions renders the actual check-run as `<wrapper-workflow-name> / <reusable-job-name>` — for SCP self this is `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. The bare `scp/policy-check` context matches only the readback status posted by the reusable workflow's commit-status step, NOT the primary check-run from the wrapper. Required-check context updated to `policy-check / scp/policy-check`. (b) **Personal-account review-shape correction:** D-032 originally set